// NODE ['Episodic']: {'entity_edges': ['f86c843d-6275-407f-bec3-1e21d0d92cd8', '22d362b2-5957-4162-a223-c2a3cfcae4e5', 'bb3f3de9-57ec-4625-bb31-2afe3e54f9ef', 'ccbca7f9-805f-4e7d-87ea-3f56d9a9c769', '4ce7b37d-7e3d-45ce-9a4f-3b347e01dc3e', '5d0a6372-6bb0-49a1-8763-cfb56f19b490', '52c4c03f-5fd7-4463-b6bd-3871d632e910', '2ceb8919-356e-4b31-b810-539da4aa4238', '81c8e15a-455d-4b37-8e4a-3f9bd4d99c22', '1a67da08-1bac-4b10-b2de-6e947befd1ee', '8dff1db1-7c44-471f-bf9a-33f0290a3e55', 'dc6f3ee6-961d-4a32-a824-6c894939f559', 'cbaa952e-5744-4798-ac74-532a8ba0da75', '32c5f99f-22e8-4b50-a71b-d6440550dc9c', 'dbff5e5d-8724-4db0-b39e-556225461c2f', 'f974d1c3-dabc-4e71-be7a-69a8fde28a92', '1ca60993-32c2-48d7-8e55-71e05d802183', '80cd3573-611c-485e-a493-6fe6538431ae', '0a67c5b6-72bc-4d98-91aa-9a32d718303e', 'f673e4a9-91fa-4205-8b17-af1721163704', '298c891e-de50-4979-9c28-f596f18b0880', 'b5bdd211-918e-42af-8ce3-d30f1b460fe8', '0e7c3508-9bbf-40b3-9d44-2ae65b0d46f7', 'bdc38b3b-5372-4cf0-a9f4-d718a6a8b6b6', '25f80fc6-dd76-4f0a-8726-8d5048f611a2', '9b7bf0ff-fec7-45a5-9c84-c8640c35e0f4', '5498ffe7-d8bb-46d6-9fe6-45115711bb49', 'fc25680d-7fe1-4c9e-a039-152c0afba9b2', '6dfdc869-ab55-4e39-a948-b0711fe52007', 'bc8b33af-d1f8-442d-a561-97aae6079e65', 'd1984f85-db52-4421-95bb-966bb7330463', '24d75b4c-e92e-42f4-a8fd-cf1af8e71493', '5a9cb957-2bbe-45d5-94f6-ed6815fc7073', '3321d7da-2d62-4cb3-adee-5a386256ace4', '0a14147b-9078-4d6d-9799-e1c203a1a7dc', '6d3b3d39-0f93-4239-bccb-c53182132c61', '4fd89c5a-588c-409b-a0d4-231992f7cfbd', '83a36a29-04a4-43a3-97a5-733e44a1eb13', '2d25caec-5a64-4e76-bc54-f90b602cd3b4', '1fd7e4a0-c023-4ff7-b46b-1baa5006fe54', 'cc8f7ee9-d9c5-47e9-a3d9-2f08a5cf27d2', '15324133-ecfc-4eab-86fd-7221edc70035', '1b118e29-398d-4884-9cc9-c80cd60e27bd', '95c89eb8-d80b-4745-8fbc-38d6b85d701d', '4e2f5d27-2042-487f-8978-3bf88c02fa5a', '4cde4b9e-60a5-4af9-b231-b95f446a0634', '759078ca-d900-4fdb-b3ad-59d9e44f62ae'], 'group_id': '', 'name': 'appendix-6-treatment.md_0_1777551626.262532', 'created_at': neo4j.time.DateTime(2026, 4, 30, 12, 20, 26, 262580000, tzinfo=<UTC>), 'source': 'text', 'uuid': '5845756d-59f8-4a33-b557-c02b27ea638d', 'content': '[Doc: APPENDIX 6: TREATMENT IN ED]\n\n# APPENDIX 6: TREATMENT IN ED  \n<!-- METADATA\ncategory: treatment_reference\nuse_case: prescribing_guidance, contraindications\nreferenced_by: section-4-treatment, section-8-special-populations\ncritical: true\n-->  \n## Mechanical Treatment  \n| Device | When/How to Apply | Precautions | Adverse Events |\n|--------|-------------------|-------------|----------------|\n| **Vacuum Erectile Devices (VED)** | 5-10 minutes before intercourse | Antiplatelets and anticoagulants - may cause bleeding and bruising | Issues with lack of spontaneity, uncomfortable, sensation of cold penis |\n| **Low-intensity Extracorporeal Shockwave Therapy (Li-ESWT)** | 20-30 minutes for each session, once a week for at least 6 sessions | - | Priapism, pain at the site, bleeding and bruising, haematuria, skin infection, painful erection, worsening penile curvature |  \n---  \n## Pharmacological Treatment (PDE5 Inhibitors)  \n### Sildenafil  \n| Parameter | Details |\n|-----------|---------|\n| **Initial Dose** | 50 mg taken approximately 1 hour before sexual activity |\n| **Effective Duration** | 30 minutes to 4 hours after administration |\n| **Half-life** | 4 hours |\n| **Dose Range** | 25-100 mg, maximum once daily |\n| **Dose Adjustments** | |\n| - Renal impairment (CrCl <30 ml/min or HD) | Starting dose 25 mg |\n| - Hepatic impairment | Starting dose 25 mg |\n| - Geriatric use | Starting dose 25 mg |\n| - Alpha-blockers | Starting dose 25 mg |\n| - Ritonavir | Maximum 25 mg over 48 hours |\n| - CYP3A4 inhibitors | Starting dose 25 mg |  \n### Tadalafil  \n| Parameter | Details |\n|-----------|---------|\n| **As Needed Dose** | 10 mg taken at least 30 minutes before sexual activity |\n| **Once Daily Dose** | 2.5 mg once daily without regard to timing of sexual activity |\n| **Effective Duration** | Up to 36 hours after administration |\n| **Half-life** | 17.5 hours |\n| **Dose Range** | As needed: 5-20 mg max once daily; Daily: 2.5-5 mg |\n| **Dose Adjustments** | |\n| - CrCl <30 ml/min or HD | Maximum 5 mg over 72 hours |\n| - Hepatic impairment (Child Pugh A/B) | Maximum 10 mg per day |\n| - Hepatic impairment (Child Pugh C) | Not recommended |\n| - CYP3A4 inhibitors | Maximum 10 mg over 72 hours |\n| - Alpha-blockers | Stable dose prior to initiation; start tadalafil at lowest dose |  \n### Avanafil  \n| Parameter | Details |\n|-----------|---------|\n| **Initial Dose** | 100 mg taken approximately 30 minutes before sexual activity |\n| **Half-life** | 5 hours |\n| **Dose Range** | 50-200 mg, maximum once daily |\n| **Dose Adjustments** | |\n| - Renal impairment (HD) | Do not use |\n| - Hepatic impairment (Child Pugh C) | Do not use |\n| - Strong CYP3A4 inhibitors | Contraindicated |\n| - Moderate CYP3A4 inhibitors | Maximum 50 mg over 24 hours |\n| - Alpha-blockers | Stable dose prior; start at 50 mg |\n| **Time to Nitrate** | 12 hours |  \n### Vardenafil  \n| Parameter | Details |\n|-----------|---------|\n| **Initial Dose** | 10 mg taken approximately 60 minutes before sexual activity |\n| **Half-life** | 4-5 hours |\n| **Dose Range** | 5-20 mg, maximum once daily |\n| **Dose Adjustments** | |\n| - HD | Do not use |\n| - Hepatic impairment (Child Pugh B) | Starting dose 5 mg, maximum 10 mg |\n| - Hepatic impairment (Child Pugh C) | Do not use |\n| - CYP3A4 inhibitors (various) | Various dose limits (see prescribing info) |\n| - Alpha-blockers | Stable dose prior; start at 5 mg |\n| - Geriatric (≥65 years) | Starting dose 5 mg |\n| **Time to Nitrate** | 24 hours |\n| **Note** | Not available in Malaysia |  \n---  \n## Contraindications (ALL PDE5i)  \n| Contraindication | Details |\n|------------------|---------|\n| Known hypersensitivity | To PDE5i or any component of tablet |\n| Nitrates/Nitrites | Concurrent use with NO donors, organic nitrates or organic nitrites (e.g. glyceryl trinitrate) |\n| Riociguat | Administration with guanylate cyclase (GC) stimulators |\n| QT prolongation (Vardenafil) | Patients with congenital QT syndrome or taking class IA/III antiarrhythmics |  \n---  \n## Adverse Events  \n| Category | Events |\n|----------|--------|\n| **Common** | Headache, flushing, dyspepsia, nasal congestion, nasopharyngitis, back pain, myalgia, visual abnormalities |\n| **Rare** | NAION (non-arteritic anterior ischemic optic neuropathy) |\n| **Serious (Vardenafil)** | QT prolongation |  \n### Warnings  \n> **Emergency:** Patients should seek emergency treatment if an erection lasts >4 hours. Use PDE5i with caution in patients predisposed to priapism.  \n> **Hearing Loss:** Patients to stop taking PDE5i and seek prompt medical attention in the event of sudden decrease or loss of hearing.  \n---  \n## Abbreviations  \n| Abbreviation | Meaning |\n|--------------|---------|\n| CrCl | Creatinine clearance |\n| HD | Haemodialysis |\n| GC | Guanylate cyclase |\n| NAION | Non-arteritic anterior ischemic optic neuropathy |\n| NO | Nitric oxide |\n| PDE5i | Phosphodiesterase-5-inhibitors |  \n---  \n**Sources:**\n1. Salonia A, et al. EAU Guidelines on Sexual and Reproductive Health. European Association of Urology; 2023.\n2. FDA Prescribing Information: CIALIS®, LEVITRA®, STENDRA®, VIAGRA®  \n---', 'valid_at': neo4j.time.DateTime(2026, 4, 30, 12, 20, 26, 262556000, tzinfo=<UTC>), 'source_description': 'Document: APPENDIX 6: TREATMENT IN ED (Chunk: 0)'}
