// NODE ['OTHER']: {'name': 'referral of patient back to primary care physician'}
// NODE ['OTHER']: {'name': 'regular communication and collaboration'}
// NODE ['Episodic']: {'entity_edges': ['b215519a-b1ea-4f0b-bae4-29e691efcb24', '7aa92147-a44f-4d78-add4-84b2c95093df', '4dc059c5-c148-4dcb-8c72-567f599f06c9'], 'group_id': '', 'name': 'section-6-followup.md_0_1777552095.079798', 'created_at': neo4j.time.DateTime(2026, 4, 30, 12, 28, 15, 79832000, tzinfo=<UTC>), 'source': 'text', 'uuid': 'a58abbc2-bbd7-414f-9b98-88f124b6a7be', 'content': "[Doc: SECTION 6: FOLLOW-UP]\n\n# SECTION 6: FOLLOW-UP  \n<!-- METADATA\ncategory: follow_up\nuse_case: treatment_monitoring, care_continuity\n-->  \n## Overview  \nThe follow-up for a patient with ED depends on the individual case and the initial treatment plan.  \n---  \n## Follow-up Types  \n### Short-term Follow-up\nFor patients initiating treatment with oral medications, a short-term follow-up within a few weeks to a couple of months may be appropriate to assess:\n- Response to medication\n- Tolerance to the medication  \n### Long-term Follow-up\nOnce a treatment plan has been established, long-term follow-up may be scheduled at regular intervals. This allows for:\n- Ongoing assessment of treatment effectiveness\n- Potential adjustments to the treatment plan\n- Monitoring for any emerging health issues  \n### As-needed Follow-up\nFor patients using on-demand treatments or lifestyle modifications, follow-up may be scheduled on an as-needed basis, depending on:\n- Their progress\n- Any changes in their health status  \n### Referral Back to Primary Care\nIf a urologist has been involved in the initial evaluation and management, the urologist may refer the patient back to his primary care physician for ongoing follow-up if the ED is stable and well-managed.  \n---  \n## Key Points  \n> **Important:** Follow-up plans will vary based on the patient's individual circumstances and response to treatment. Regular communication and collaboration between the primary care physician and the urologist, if involved, are key components of effective care for individuals with ED.  \n---", 'valid_at': neo4j.time.DateTime(2026, 4, 30, 12, 28, 15, 79813000, tzinfo=<UTC>), 'source_description': 'Document: SECTION 6: FOLLOW-UP (Chunk: 0)'}
// NODE ['Episodic']: {'entity_edges': ['501494bc-bc93-4347-b1cf-2e09e8ccaf67', '717495ce-affc-4a15-a6f6-c7ff45767081', '22946482-6f4a-47f4-81c2-41ee2d545a52', 'fa221059-3c7a-43a5-baa4-07cfa9b8af01', 'ad10135c-a51f-4516-a7dd-164a6264e36e', '7aa92147-a44f-4d78-add4-84b2c95093df', 'b215519a-b1ea-4f0b-bae4-29e691efcb24'], 'group_id': '', 'name': 'section-7-referral.md_0_1777552114.23137', 'created_at': neo4j.time.DateTime(2026, 4, 30, 12, 28, 34, 231415000, tzinfo=<UTC>), 'source': 'text', 'uuid': '79aab7a4-7597-4a57-ade7-e4cff3304473', 'content': '[Doc: SECTION 7: REFERRAL]\n\n# SECTION 7: REFERRAL  \n<!-- METADATA\ncategory: referral\nuse_case: specialist_consultation, care_coordination\n-->  \n## Overview  \nReferring a patient with ED to a urologist or other relevant specialist is typically considered in the following situations:  \n---  \n## Referral Indications  \n### 1. Primary Care Evaluation\nThe primary care physician has assessed the patient, taken a detailed medical history and performed a physical examination. If the underlying cause of ED is not evident or if there are concerns about specific urological issues, a referral may be appropriate.  \n### 2. Treatment Failure or Complexity\nIf initial treatments (e.g. lifestyle changes, oral medications like PDE5i, or other conservative measures) do not yield satisfactory results, or if a case is complex and may require specialised interventions:\n- Penile injections\n- Vacuum Erection Devices (VEDs)\n- Surgical options  \nA urologist may be consulted.  \n### 3. Underlying Medical Conditions\nPresence of co-morbidities that might contribute to or exacerbate ED:\n- Diabetes mellitus\n- Cardiovascular disease\n- Hormonal disorders  \nConsultation with a urologist and/or endocrinologist/cardiologist may be warranted.  \n### 4. Psychological Factors\nIf psychological factors are suspected to be a significant contributor to the ED, collaboration with a mental health professional may be necessary. However, urologists may still play a role in addressing any physical aspects of the condition.  \n---', 'valid_at': neo4j.time.DateTime(2026, 4, 30, 12, 28, 34, 231397000, tzinfo=<UTC>), 'source_description': 'Document: SECTION 7: REFERRAL (Chunk: 0)'}
